    "answer": {
      "short": "$y = [1, 4, 7, 10, 13]$; equation: $y=3x+1$",
      "worked": "Substitute each value of $x$ into the equation $y = 3x + 1$:\n- For $x = 0$: $y = 3(0) + 1 = 1$\n- For $x = 1$: $y = 3(1) + 1 = 4$\n- For $x = 2$: $y = 3(2) + 1 = 7$\n- For $x = 3$: $y = 3(3) + 1 = 10$\n- For $x = 4$: $y = 3(4) + 1 = 13$\n\nPlot the coordinates $(0, 1), (1, 4), (2, 7), (3, 10), (4, 13)$ on the Cartesian plane and join with a straight line.",
